Done! The recipe now builds on `provide()`/`inject()`, thanks for the nudge (and for #3512, it fits this component like a glove).

`InputOtp` provides `inputs` and `name`, and each `Slot` only declares its `input` position: the accessible "Input X of Y" label and the default `name` are derived from the context, so the `inputs="6" name="otp[...]"` repetition is gone from every example.

The branch predated the new Toolkit conventions, so I also migrated the recipe while I was at it: README-based examples, `tailwind_classes` merging, `@prop` docblocks, and `ux:toolkit:lint-kit` is green. Snapshots regenerated, 610 rendering tests pass locally.

